.dotmd/

# The planning tree is NOT public. dotmd is developed by running it against a
# large private corpus, so its own plans, prompts and audits accumulate consumer
# detail as a matter of course — that is what makes them good planning documents
# and what makes them unpublishable. This repo is public, so the tree stays on
# disk and out of the index.
#
# Chosen over a private nested repo (two repos to commit in for one change) and
# over making the whole repo private (dotmd is a published package; losing public
# source presence costs more than the history is worth). git-crypt was rejected
# on foot-gun: a fresh clone without the filter configured commits plaintext
# silently, which is the wrong failure mode for the thing whose job is not
# leaking.
#
# `docs/` keeps its normal path, so repoRoot containment and every config default
# are untouched. Anything that should be publicly readable goes OUTSIDE this tree
# rather than being carved out as an exception — README.md already carries usage.
# See docs/plans/sanitize-public-repo.md § Phase 3.
/docs/
